# labwc reads this along with /etc/xdg/labwc/environment (elavo-session runs
# labwc --merge-config), before wlroots opens the GPU.
#
# wlroots finds NVIDIA's GBM backend on its own (Mesa's libgbm loads
# nvidia-drm_gbm.so by DRM driver name), so GBM_BACKEND is not set. It,
# __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME and LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME are also left alone
# because forcing them breaks laptops where Intel or AMD graphics drive
# the panel and the NVIDIA GPU is the second one.
#
# The hardware cursor plane has shown an invisible or frozen cursor on
# NVIDIA with wlroots. A software cursor avoids that at a small cost.
# Take this line out once it is checked on real hardware.
WLR_NO_HARDWARE_CURSORS=1
